From 882537f807315bcef83d21d95da561ee2d704c8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NVR <rkwastavich@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:40:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] NVR extension 1.1: full-screen graphics passes (own
 SPIR-V fragment/vertex shaders, up to 4 targets, viewport, blend)

CreateGraphicsPipeline/Draw record a full-screen triangle through DxvkContext with the
extension's own render targets, viewport, rasterizer/blend/depth state and bindings, then
put the whole context state back (dxvk_context.h: nvrGetState/nvrSetState) so D3D9's state
is re-applied at its next draw. Built-in vertex shader d3d9_nvr_fullscreen_vert.vert.
Written storage buffers now go through raw buffer views so their writes are tracked (a
readback or copy could otherwise be moved in front of the dispatch).
